@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Supplier update — lorry hire details
+
+Depends on: the `Supplier` model fields already on `main` (`supplierType`, `panNumber`, `defaultTdsRate`, `tdsDeclaration`, `bankDetails`).
+
+Why: the lorry hire form already reads these from a saved supplier to pre-fill itself, but nothing could set them — the Suppliers routes and modal ignored them, so they only got a PAN/type when auto-created from a contract.
+
+Scope
+1. `lib/supplier/extras.ts` — shared (client + server) parser/validator for the new fields. Only keys present in a request are applied, so an older client never wipes them; a blank default TDS clears it. A 194C(6) declaration requires a valid PAN.
+2. `lib/supplier/service.ts` — create / update / delete logic; routes in `app/api/admin/supplier/*` are now thin wrappers (same response shapes; create/update still answer 200 for the Redux slice).
+   - Duplicate names are matched case-insensitively (same rule the lorry hire form uses to link a typed supplier).
+   - Renaming refreshes the party name on the supplier's ledger `Payment` rows. Issued contracts keep the name they were issued with.
+   - A supplier with active (non-cancelled) contracts can't be deleted (409).
+3. `GET /api/admin/supplier/get` also searches PAN and accepts `supplierType=Broker|Owner` (suppliers without a type count as Broker).
+4. Suppliers page: Type + PAN columns and a "Lorry hire details" section in the modal (`components/lorry-hire/SupplierLorryHireFields.tsx`) with a suggested TDS rate, declaration checkbox and bank details. Form mapping lives in `lib/supplier/form.ts`.
+5. Lorry hire form: picking a supplier with a saved 194C(6) declaration (and a valid PAN) starts the contract at 0% TDS.
+6. `lib/company-filter.ts` — `companyFilter` moved out of `company-scope.ts` (re-exported, no behaviour change) so data-layer code can be imported and tested without next-auth.
+
+Tests: `npm test`. The integration tests in `lib/supplier/__tests__/service.int.test.ts` need a MongoDB and are skipped unless `TEST_MONGODB_URI` is set, e.g.
+`TEST_MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017 npm test` (each run uses a throw-away database).
